              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.2: Some possible criteria of groupings of plants and animals"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.192,
            0.744,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have grouped animals based on varied features, such as what they eat, where they live, what colour they are and how they move."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.252,
            0.744,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the importance of grouping? Grouping makes it easier to understand and study plants and animals on the basis of their similarities and differences."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.311,
            0.743,
            0.352
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You will learn more about the importance of grouping in our daily lives in the chapter, ‘Materials Around Us’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.367,
            0.434,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.2.1 How to group plants?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.399,
            0.744,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You must have noticed that plants show variation in the features related to stems, leaves, flowers, and more. The stems of different plants vary in thickness, height, and hardness, while the leaves vary in shape, colour, size and arrangement. You might have tried grouping the plants in Activity 2.3 using one of these features."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.518,
            0.744,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have also learnt in earlier classes that plants can be grouped into herbs, shrubs, and trees based on their height and types of stem. Let us study the features of plants in more detail and group them on that basis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.61,
            0.391,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.4: Let us group"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.637,
            0.743,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us go on a nature walk again for some more interesting observations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.682,
            0.744,
            0.743
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Look closely at the height of different plants. Are these plants shorter than you, as tall as you, or taller than you?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.748,
            0.744,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the stem brown or green? Touch and feel the stems and try to bend them gently. Can you bend the stem easily, or is it stiff? Take care that the stems do not break."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.813,
            0.744,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Also, observe from where the branches of the plants arise—whether they arise close to the ground or higher up on the stem. Fill in your observations in Table 2.3. A few examples are already given."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.889,
            0.715,
            0.91,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Diversity in the Living World"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 14,
